---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Show an entity's thread along its kind's route, its traceability chain, or every entity's

Usage: specforge trace [OPTIONS] [ENTITY]

Arguments:
  [ENTITY]
          Entity ID to trace (omit to trace every entity)

Options:
      --plan <FILE>
          An agent plan file (an AgentPlan's JSON) to check against the graph instead of tracing

      --route <NAME>
          Follow this route (its qualified name, `<extension>/<route>`); with no entity, trace every entity of its start kind

      --reach
          Trace the entity's reach both ways, whatever route starts at its kind

      --partial
          Print a route's thread even when it is incomplete, with a `no <step>` marker where it falls short

      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json (default: human for a route's thread, json otherwise)
          
          [possible values: human, json]

  -h, --help
          Print help
